  "text": "Deborah ran a nation from under a palm tree. Judges chapter four. Deborah is a prophetess, and she is judging Israel at the time, and she holds court under a palm tree between Ramah and Bethel. The children of Israel come up to her for judgement. That is her office. That is her authority, written down, no hedging. So she summons Barak and gives him God's orders. Take ten thousand men to mount Tabor. I will draw out Sisera and his chariots to the river Kishon and deliver him into thine hand. And Barak, the military commander, says, if thou wilt go with me, then I will go. But if thou wilt not go with me, then I will not go. He will not move without her. So she goes. And she tells him plainly, the journey that thou takest shall not be for thine honour, for the Lord shall sell Sisera into the hand of a woman. She called the ending before it happened, and it landed exactly the way she said. She held court under a tree, and the nation came to her.",
